  "name": "Scholarly Prompt Lab: The Prompt as Method",
  "description": "Design, document and examine how scholarly knowledge develops through human–AI interaction. Free and open-source research software for the humanities and social sciences. It supports single-prompt analysis, four-condition prompt-sensitivity studies and documented multi-turn research conversations (the SPL Research Session Protocol and the Research Session Record), organised by the CONTEXT framework. Runs in the browser; research data stays on the researcher's device.",
